                s("How PMI Thinks — The Core Mental Model", "• Proactive always beats reactive. If two answers look similar, pick the one that anticipates the problem rather than reacts to it.\n• A.R.T. sequence: Assess/Analyze → Review project documents → Take Action. Never jump straight to action.\n• Communicate first. Before any drastic action, communicate with stakeholders.\n• Collaborate, don't escalate. Escalate to the sponsor only when the issue is beyond the PM's authority, after you've tried to resolve it internally.\n• Process always applies. Even for \"small\" changes — Integrated Change Control, no exceptions.\n• Never fire/hire/terminate as a first response. Never as a second either.\n• Never bypass the team. PM does not delegate PM responsibilities to others.\n• Safety first — always. Safety issues stop all other work immediately.\n• The team estimates. The PM does not estimate for the team — SMEs provide estimates.\n• Face-to-face is best. For conflict, sensitive topics, and complex issues, always prefer face-to-face interaction."),
