                s("Pre-Exam Preparation Checklist", "• Formulas to memorise: CPI, SPI, EV, EAC (all 4 versions), TCPI, PERT, Channels, EMV, PTA\n• Sequences to memorise: Control Quality → Validate Scope. Formal acceptance → Lessons Learned → Release team → Archive → Close contracts\n• TKI order: Collaborate → Compromise → Smooth → Force → Avoid\n• Power types order: Expert → Referent → Reward → Legitimate → Penalty\n• Tuckman stages: Forming → Storming → Norming → Performing → Adjourning\n• Risk responses: Escalate, Avoid/Exploit, Transfer/Share, Mitigate/Enhance, Accept (Active/Passive)\n• Contract types by risk: FFP (seller) → FPIF → T&M → CPIF → CPFF (buyer)\n• ADKAR: Awareness → Desire → Knowledge → Ability → Reinforcement\n• On exam day: Write ALL formulas on scratch paper the moment you sit down. Do this BEFORE reading the first question."),
