                s("Key PMBOK 8 Terminology — Know These Definitions", tableHeaders = listOf("Term", "PMBOK 8 Definition"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Artifact", "A template, document, output, or project deliverable. A product is an artifact that is produced, quantifiable, and can be an end item or component."), listOf("Deliverable", "Any unique and verifiable product, result, or capability to perform a service that is required to be produced to complete a process, phase, or project."), listOf("Outcome", "An end result or consequence of a process or project. Outcomes can include outputs and artifacts but have broader intent — focused on benefits and value."), listOf("Value", "The worth, importance, or usefulness of something. Different stakeholders perceive value differently — financial, social, environmental, reputational."), listOf("Benefit", "A gain realised by the organisation and beneficiaries through project outputs and resulting outcomes."), listOf("Disbenefit", "A negative consequence of project outputs — must be identified and managed alongside benefits (new in PMBOK 8 vocabulary)."), listOf("Project Management Team", "Members of the project team directly involved in project management activities (broader than just the PM)."), listOf("Development Approach", "The method used to create and evolve the product, service, or result — predictive, adaptive, or hybrid."), listOf("Life Cycle", "The series of phases a project passes through from start to completion. Different from the development approach."), listOf("Tailoring", "The deliberate adaptation of the PM approach, governance, and processes to make them more suitable for the given environment."))),
                s("Project Success — PMBOK 8 Criteria", "PMBOK 8 defines project success beyond the traditional iron triangle:"),
                s("Project Success — PMBOK 8 Criteria", tableHeaders = listOf("Traditional (PMBOK 6)", "Modern (PMBOK 8)"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("On time", "Delivered when needed — cadence matters more than a single date"), listOf("On budget", "Investment justified by value delivered — not just spend control"), listOf("Within scope", "Delivered the RIGHT scope — outcomes achieved, not just outputs"), listOf("—", "Benefits realised (during and after project)"), listOf("—", "Stakeholder satisfaction (including end users)"), listOf("—", "Sustainability impact (people, profit, planet)"), listOf("—", "Organisational learning captured"))),
                s("Worked example — The 6 Principles — Applied to a Real Project Situation", "Project: Implementing AI-powered credit scoring for a microfinance institution serving rural borrowers\n\nPrinciple 1 — Adopt a Holistic View:\n\nThe team notices the AI model is trained on urban credit bureau data. Rural borrowers have different financial patterns (agricultural income cycles, informal credit). A holistic view reveals the model may systematically deny credit to exactly the customers the institution wants to serve.\n\n→ Expand the model training to include rural financial behaviour data before launch.\n\nPrinciple 2 — Focus on Value:\n\nThe project's KPI is \"number of loan applications processed per day.\" The PM flags that processing 500 applications efficiently but approving 400 incorrect ones destroys value. Reframe the KPI to \"default rate\" and \"customer satisfaction\" — the actual value drivers.\n\nPrinciple 3 — Embed Quality:\n\nRather than testing the AI model only at the end, add bias-testing checkpoints after every training iteration. Make \"fairness metrics across demographic groups\" part of the Definition of Done for each model version.\n\nPrinciple 4 — Be an Accountable Leader:\n\nWhen a team member discovers the model makes errors on agricultural borrowers, the PM does not blame the data scientist. She takes ownership: \"We did not include this in our test cases. I own that. Here is how we fix it.\" This creates safety to surface problems early.\n\nPrinciple 5 — Integrate Sustainability:\n\nThe institution serves 50,000 rural borrowers. A biased model that denies credit to creditworthy rural women would have profound social impact (disbenefits). The PM documents both the financial benefit AND the social risk in the Benefits Management Plan.\n\nPrinciple 6 — Build an Empowered Culture:\n\nThe junior data scientist noticed the bias issue but was afraid to raise it. After the PM's Principle 4 response, he feels safe to raise two more concerns in the next sprint. The team's best ideas are now accessible.", SectionKind.TIP),
                s("Worked example — Focus Areas (Process Groups) — What They Look Like in Practice", "Project: Building a mobile-first insurance claims app (hybrid approach)\n\nINITIATING:\n\n• Sponsor signs Project Charter authorising ₹2.5 crore budget\n\n• PM and sponsor agree on success criteria: \"70% of claims submitted digitally within 6 months of launch\"\n\n• Initial stakeholder identification: policyholders, claim adjusters, IT team, legal/compliance, call centre\n\n• Assumption Log created: \"Average claim takes 7 days to process today; target is 3 days\"\n\nPLANNING:\n\n• PM Plan integrated: scope, schedule, cost, quality, risk, resource, communications, stakeholder, procurement plans\n\n• Baselines: WBS approved (22 epics → 180 user stories); Schedule baseline: 18 months; Cost baseline: ₹2.2 crore (₹30L contingency above)\n\n• Risk Register: 18 risks identified; 4 high-priority; contingency plans for top 3\n\nEXECUTING:\n\n• Sprint 1–3: Claims submission flow (predictive infrastructure running in parallel)\n\n• Manage Quality: two UX usability tests with actual policyholders; team adjusts form flow after feedback\n\n• Vendor (OCR engine for document scanning) contracted using CPIF to incentivise accuracy\n\nMONITORING & CONTROLLING (runs throughout):\n\n• Sprint 6: SPI = 0.91 (slightly behind). PM analyzes: one backend developer out sick for 2 weeks. Corrective action: redistribute tasks; no change request needed as contingency buffer absorbs.\n\n• Sprint 11: Compliance team raises new RBI data localisation requirement. Change request raised; +₹18L, +3 weeks approved by CCB.\n\nCLOSING:\n\n• UAT completed; 94% of test cases passed (above 90% threshold)\n\n• Formal acceptance signed by Head of Claims\n\n• Lessons learned workshop: 3 retrospective improvement ideas adopted into the PMO's standard playbook\n\n• Team disbanded; transition document handed to operations\n\n• Benefits tracking begun: adoption rate 34% in Month 1 (target 70% by Month 6)", SectionKind.TIP),
                s("PMBOK 8 vs PMBOK 7 vs PMBOK 6 — Complete Comparison Table", tableHeaders = listOf("Aspect", "PMBOK 6 (2017)", "PMBOK 7 (2021)", "PMBOK 8 (2025)"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Core Structure", "49 Processes + 10 Knowledge Areas", "12 Principles + 8 Performance Domains", "6 Principles + 7 Domains + 40 Processes"), listOf("Process Groups", "5 explicit (Initiating through Closing)", "Removed — described as a separate guide", "Reintroduced as 5 Focus Areas within guide"), listOf("ITTOs", "Central — detailed inputs, tools, outputs for all 49 processes", "Removed from main guide", "Reintegrated into domain processes"), listOf("Quality", "Separate Knowledge Area (Ch.8)", "Within Delivery domain", "Within Governance domain"), listOf("Communications", "Separate KA (Ch.10)", "Within Stakeholders domain", "Merged into Stakeholders domain"), listOf("Procurement", "Separate KA (Ch.12)", "Distributed across domains", "Across Resources + Governance"), listOf("AI Guidance", "Not mentioned", "Brief mention", "Dedicated task (Business Environment B7)"), listOf("Sustainability", "Not explicit", "Brief mention", "Dedicated principle (Principle 5) + dedicated task (B8)"), listOf("Lifecycle Bias", "Predictive-heavy", "Agnostic", "Fully agnostic, agile-forward"), listOf("Agile Coverage", "Brief appendix", "Central", "Integrated throughout all domains"), listOf("Process Count", "49", "~14 practices", "40 non-prescriptive processes"), listOf("Edition", "6th (2017)", "7th (2021)", "8th (2025)"))),
                s("All 40 PMBOK 8 Processes — Full Reference", tableHeaders = listOf("#", "Process Name", "Domain", "Focus Area", "Primary Output"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("1", "Initiate Project or Phase", "Governance", "Initiating", "Project Charter, Initial Assumption Log"), listOf("2", "Integrate and Align Project Plans", "Governance", "Planning", "Project Management Plan (integrated)"), listOf("3", "Plan Sourcing Strategy", "Governance", "Planning", "Procurement Strategy, Make-or-Buy decisions"), listOf("4", "Manage Project Execution", "Governance", "Executing", "Deliverables, Work Performance Data"), listOf("5", "Manage Quality Assurance", "Governance", "Executing", "Quality Reports, Process Improvements"), listOf("6", "Manage Project Knowledge", "Governance", "Executing", "Lessons Learned Register updates, OPA updates"), listOf("7", "Monitor and Control Project Performance", "Governance", "M&C", "Work Performance Reports, Change Requests"), listOf("8", "Assess and Implement Changes", "Governance", "M&C", "Approved Changes, Change Log, Plan Updates"), listOf("9", "Close Project or Phase", "Governance", "Closing", "Final Report, Closed Contracts, OPA updates"), listOf("10", "Plan Scope Management", "Scope", "Planning", "Scope Management Plan"), listOf("11", "Elicit and Analyse Requirements", "Scope", "Planning", "Requirements Documentation, RTM"), listOf("12", "Define Scope", "Scope", "Planning", "Project Scope Statement"), listOf("13", "Develop Scope Structure", "Scope", "Planning", "WBS, WBS Dictionary (Scope Baseline)"), listOf("14", "Validate Scope", "Scope", "M&C", "Accepted Deliverables"), listOf("15", "Monitor and Control Scope", "Scope", "M&C", "Work Performance Information, Change Requests"), listOf("16", "Plan Schedule Management", "Schedule", "Planning", "Schedule Management Plan"), listOf("17", "Develop Schedule", "Schedule", "Planning", "Project Schedule, Schedule Baseline"), listOf("18", "Monitor and Control Schedule", "Schedule", "M&C", "Work Performance Information, Change Requests"), listOf("19", "Plan Financial Management", "Finance", "Planning", "Financial Management Plan"), listOf("20", "Estimate Costs", "Finance", "Planning", "Cost Estimates, Basis of Estimates"), listOf("21", "Develop Budget", "Finance", "Planning", "Cost Baseline, Project Funding Requirements"), listOf("22", "Monitor and Control Finances", "Finance", "M&C", "Work Performance Information, Change Requests"), listOf("23", "Identify Stakeholders", "Stakeholders", "Initiating", "Stakeholder Register"), listOf("24", "Plan Stakeholder Engagement", "Stakeholders", "Planning", "Stakeholder Engagement Plan"), listOf("25", "Plan Communications Management", "Stakeholders", "Planning", "Communications Management Plan"), listOf("26", "Manage Stakeholder Engagement", "Stakeholders", "Executing", "Change Requests, OPA updates"), listOf("27", "Manage Communications", "Stakeholders", "Executing", "Project Communications, OPA updates"), listOf("28", "Monitor Stakeholder Engagement", "Stakeholders", "M&C", "Work Performance Information, Change Requests"), listOf("29", "Monitor Communications", "Stakeholders", "M&C", "Work Performance Information"), listOf("30", "Plan Resource Management", "Resources", "Planning", "Resource Management Plan"), listOf("31", "Estimate Resources", "Resources", "Planning", "Resource Requirements, Resource Breakdown Structure"), listOf("32", "Acquire Resources", "Resources", "Executing", "Physical Resource Assignments, Project Team Assignments"), listOf("33", "Lead the Team", "Resources", "Executing", "Team Performance Assessments, Change Requests"), listOf("34", "Monitor and Control Resourcing", "Resources", "M&C", "Work Performance Information, Change Requests"), listOf("35", "Plan Risk Management", "Risk", "Planning", "Risk Management Plan"), listOf("36", "Identify Risks", "Risk", "Planning", "Risk Register"), listOf("37", "Perform Risk Analysis", "Risk", "Planning", "Risk Report, Priority Risk List"), listOf("38", "Plan Risk Responses", "Risk", "Planning", "Risk Register updates, Risk Report updates"), listOf("39", "Implement Risk Responses", "Risk", "Executing", "Change Requests, Risk Register updates"), listOf("40", "Monitor Risks", "Risk", "M&C", "Work Performance Information, Change Requests"))),
                s("All 40 PMBOK 8 Processes — Full Reference", "Only the GOVERNANCE domain has processes in ALL five Focus Areas. All other domains skip Initiating (except Stakeholders) and Closing. This is frequently tested.", SectionKind.KEY),
                s("PMBOK 8 Principles — Deep Dive with Exam Application", tableHeaders = listOf("Principle", "Core Concept", "Exam Application", "Anti-Pattern (wrong answer)"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("1. Adopt a Holistic View", "Think systemically — consider all stakeholders, environment, interrelationships, and second-order effects", "When a question shows a decision that optimises one metric but harms others, the holistic view would catch this", "Focusing only on cost/schedule without considering quality, stakeholder impact, or sustainability"), listOf("2. Focus on Value", "Every decision, activity, and deliverable must be justified by the value it creates — for stakeholders and the organisation", "When asked \"should we continue this project?\" — evaluate value, not sunk costs", "Measuring success by triple constraint alone — on time, on budget, but zero adoption = failure"), listOf("3. Embed Quality", "Quality is planned and built in — not inspected in at the end. Continuous improvement.", "Prevention cost questions — always prefer preventing over fixing. DoD in agile = quality built in", "Allowing a deliverable to ship that \"looks fine\" without verification against specifications"), listOf("4. Be an Accountable Leader", "Lead with integrity. Share leadership — any team member can lead. Foster psychological safety.", "When asked about leadership style: servant leadership for empowered teams. Own your mistakes.", "Autocratic decision-making as default. Blame culture. Hiding mistakes."), listOf("5. Integrate Sustainability", "People, profit, planet. Short-term and long-term. Consider community, society, future generations.", "Any question about environmental impact, social impact, ESG, or disbenefits connects here", "Ignoring negative social/environmental consequences because they are \"outside project scope\""), listOf("6. Build an Empowered Culture", "Mutual trust, clear roles, collaborative objectives. Empowered teams maximise value.", "Team charter questions. Autonomy vs control. Empowerment vs micromanagement.", "Centralising all decisions with the PM. Not involving team in planning or estimation."))),
                s("Delivery Cadence — Choosing the Right Approach", tableHeaders = listOf("Factor", "Predictive", "Iterative", "Incremental", "Agile", "Hybrid"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Requirements clarity", "Very clear and stable", "Partially clear; may evolve", "Clear about WHAT; HOW is refined", "Unclear; emerges over time", "Mixed — some clear, some unclear"), listOf("Change rate", "Low — changes are expensive", "Moderate — planned iterations", "Low per increment", "High — change is expected and welcome", "Varies by component"), listOf("Delivery timing", "Single delivery at end", "Multiple versions of same deliverable", "Partial but usable deliverables over time", "Frequent small deliveries, always usable", "Different cadences per component"), listOf("Stakeholder involvement", "At milestones/gates", "At end of each iteration", "At each increment delivery", "Continuous collaboration", "Varies by component"), listOf("Risk approach", "Identify and plan upfront", "Revisit each iteration", "Reduce risk incrementally", "Risk managed per sprint", "Both formal and iterative"), listOf("Best for", "Construction, manufacturing, regulated", "R&D, software prototyping", "Large software releases, hardware", "Software, services, innovation", "Complex projects with multiple workstreams"), listOf("PMBOK 8 example", "Building a bridge", "Drug development phases", "ERP module releases", "Mobile app development", "Bank system with hardware + software"))),
                s("Organisational Governance Structures and Their Impact", tableHeaders = listOf("Structure", "Definition", "PM Authority", "Resource Control", "Typical Industries"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Organic/Simple", "No formal structure; owner manages everything", "None — owner makes all decisions", "Owner controls all", "Micro-businesses, family businesses"), listOf("Functional", "Organised by function (IT, Finance, HR); functional managers rule", "Little to none; PM is coordinator", "Functional Manager controls", "Manufacturing, government, military"), listOf("Weak Matrix", "PM role exists but FM is dominant", "Low — PM is coordinator or facilitator", "Functional Manager dominant", "Large corporations in transition"), listOf("Balanced Matrix", "Power shared between PM and FM", "Moderate — shared authority", "Negotiated between PM and FM", "Consulting firms, professional services"), listOf("Strong Matrix", "PM has significant authority; PM is full-time", "Moderate to High", "PM dominant", "IT companies, engineering firms"), listOf("Project-Oriented", "Organisation structured around projects; PMs have full authority", "High to Almost Total", "PM controls", "Construction, aerospace, defence"), listOf("PMO Structure", "PMO manages the portfolio; PM staff from PMO", "High to Almost Total", "PMO controls allocation", "Large enterprise, programme management"), listOf("Virtual", "Geographically dispersed; technology-enabled", "Varies", "Technology-dependent", "Global IT, outsourcing, modern enterprises"))),
